        "tree_id": "1b92a2910c383d11d78b18be09f01643cbcb6e45",
        "message": "fix(41): the glyphs were right but too small and too close for ML Kit\n\nRun 36594946025, with the font rows fixed:\n\n    ocr -> INVOICE INY-447 DUE 2926-03-01\n\nwhich is a long way from\n\n    IMJOICE IMYAA71 DUE 2926-03-g1\n\nthree characters out. INVOICE is now exact. What is left is not a font bug:\n\n  - \"4471\" came back as \"447\": the trailing 1 merged into the 7\n  - \"2026\" came back as \"2926\": the 0 read as a 9\n  - V grew a tail from the adjacent hyphen\n\nAll three are spacing and shape at scale=6, gap=2, which is 30 pixels of glyph\nwith 12 pixels of gap. --show prints the same glyphs and they are correct, so the\nshapes are right and the rendering is too tight for a text recogniser.\n\n  - scale 6 -> 8 and gap 2 -> 4. Larger, and four cell-widths between glyphs\n    instead of two, so nothing can borrow a stroke from its neighbour.\n  - \"0\" now uses a CENTRE BAR instead of a diagonal slash. A diagonal inside an\n    oval is a classic misread; a vertical bar is what a recogniser expects for a\n    zero and keeps it distinct from O.\n\nVerified with --show again, reading the pixels directly: I N V O I C E 4 4 7 1\n2 0 2 6 - 0 3 - 0 1 are all correct.\n\nML Kit, the Tesseract path, and the native runOcr stub are all behaving. The\nremaining risk is that 810 pixels of 5x7 bitmap at 8x is still thin for OCR, and\nif the next run is still short I will render at a larger scale with a plainer\nfont rather than keep tuning glyphs.",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-29T16:25:38Z",
